      Order calculation requires explicit `lifecycleOperation` before starting `orderCalculationPipeline`, preserving historical checkout evidence unless a governed amendment, return, refund, adjustment, or reconciliation operation allows recalculation.
      `DefaultOrderCalculationPipelineService.calculateEntries` executes `orderEntryCalculationPipeline` once per order entry and stores calculated-entry evidence in the aggregate pipeline result.
      Validation run: `node gComm/cart/test/cartCalculationPipelineContract.test.js`, `node gComm/order/test/orderCalculationPipelineContract.test.js`, `node gComm/order/test/checkoutPlacementWorkflowPipelineContract.test.js`, `node gComm/cart/test/cartEntryFoundationContract.test.js`, `node gComm/cart/test/cartCheckoutAllocationFoundationContract.test.js`, `node gComm/order/test/orderEntryFoundationContract.test.js`, `npm run structure:audit -- --fail`, `npm run module:metadata`, `npm run llm:generate`, and `npm run llm:validate`.

