  ☐ Decide Point of Service relation to store, warehouse, pickup capacity, address, geolocation, opening hours, inventory, and delivery mode. @p2 @commerce
    Current evidence 2026-08-02:
      `store` and `storeWarehouseAssignment` provide store, warehouse assignment, channels, capabilities, address reference, and external references. A dedicated Point of Service model with pickup capacity, geolocation/opening-hour contract, delivery-mode relation, and operational lifecycle is not yet defined.
      Validation run for current foundation: `node gComm/store/test/storeFoundationService.test.js` and `node gComm/store/test/storeWarehouseReferenceProvider.test.js`.
  ☐ Add order cancellation configuration: cancellable states, line-level cancellation, payment void/refund, stock release, fulfillment cancellation, and customer notification. @p2 @commerce
    Current evidence 2026-08-02:
      Checkout compensation can cancel Fulfillment release and Inventory has reservation/allocation cancellation intents. A complete order-cancellation business capability, including line-level cancellation, Payment void/refund routing, stock release, Fulfillment cancellation, customer notification, and Order history, still needs dedicated design.
  ☐ Add quotes and quote entries for B2B/assisted-sales after cart/order foundation is stable. @p2 @commerce
    Current evidence 2026-08-02:
      No first-class Quote or Quote Entry backend model was found in current Commerce modules. This remains a B2B/assisted-sales workstream.
